# go-deps-view layers, top first.
# Each entry is a folder or package path; "*" (quoted) means everything not listed.
# The graph is a star: features and providers both import the root contracts and
# never each other; the application (here zarf/examples) picks the provider.
layers:
  - name: Contracts
    description: The root package, stdlib only; every arrow ends here
    packages: [.]

  - name: Features
    description: What consumers import; they take a sense port, never a provider
    entrypoint: true
    packages: [search, tagging]

  - name: Providers
    description: Local model runtimes that implement the sense ports
    packages: [provider]

  - name: Foundation
    description: Vector stores, media ports and shared internals
    packages: ["*"]

  - name: Support
    description: Examples, evaluation and test fakes
    packages: [zarf, sensetest]

# Toggled off until someone clicks them or "show all": the Support paths plus
# the EmbeddingCache conformance suite, test code that sits under tagging.
hidden: [zarf, sensetest, tagging/cachetest]

# Text shown by a package's or library's "i" button.
info:
  .: |
    The module's contracts (ports), not data structs.

    Embedder, ImageEmbedder and Completer are the interfaces the providers
    implement and the features consume. Role tells an Embedder whether a text is
    a query or a document. LazyEmbedder defers loading a model until first use.

    Everything imports this package and it imports only the standard library, so
    a feature never depends on a provider: the application picks one and passes
    it in.

    The interfaces live here, not in each consumer, because Embed takes a Role:
    providers and consumers need one shared Role type, and Embedder has several
    consumers. Keep it stdlib-only; if it ever needs a provider, ffmpeg or a
    store, split it.

  search: |
    Semantic search over opaque document ids: embeds text, images and video
    segments through the sense ports and stores the vectors in a vector.Store.
    Knows nothing about what the documents are.

  tagging: |
    Suggests tags for texts: a Tagger chooses among an application's existing
    tags (by embedding), a Generator writes new ones (through a Completer).
    Reads the application's tags through a Catalog; keeps only an embedding
    cache (MemCache, pgcache, sqlitecache) and an in-memory tag index.

  provider/yzma: |
    GGUF models through llama.cpp: a text Embedder, a Completer, and the Vision
    embedder (Qwen3-VL), which puts text, images and video segments in one space.

  provider/onnx: ONNX Runtime image models as a sense.ImageEmbedder.

  vector: |
    The vector.Store port plus MemStore, an in-memory store for tests and small
    corpora. pgvec and sqlitevec are the SQL implementations.

  media: |
    Ports for video input: Sampler (frames), VideoEmbedder (segments) and Cutter.
    media/ffmpeg implements them over the ffmpeg binaries.

  internal/fetch: Downloads and verifies the providers' native libraries and models.
  internal/hw: Detects the machine's accelerators so a provider can pick a runtime build.
  internal/tablename: Derives the per-index physical table names of the SQL stores.
  sensetest: Fakes of the sense ports, for this module's tests and its users'.
